---
description: Depot Third Party Package Overlays
globs: *.nix
---
# Depot Third Party Package Overlays

Rules for creating and maintaining third-party package overlays in the depot repository.

<rule>
name: third_party_overlay
description: Standards for creating new third-party package overlays
filters:
  - type: file_path
    pattern: "third_party/.*/default\\.nix$"
actions:
  - type: reject
    conditions:
      - pattern: "^[^#]"
        message: "License header missing at file start"
      - pattern: "pkgs\\.PACKAGE_NAME"
        message: "PACKAGE_NAME placeholder must be replaced with actual package name"
      - pattern: "pkgs\\.[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+(?!\\.overrideAttrs)"
        message: "Must use overrideAttrs for package customization"
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      Follow these conventions when creating a new third-party package overlay:

      1. Create a new directory under third_party/ named after the package
      2. Create a default.nix with this minimal structure:
         ```nix
         # Copyright (c) YEAR Geoffrey Huntley <ghuntley@ghuntley.com>. All rights reserved.
         # SPDX-License-Identifier: Proprietary

         { pkgs, ... }:

         pkgs.PACKAGE_NAME.overrideAttrs (old: {
           # Add custom patches if needed
           patches = (old.patches or []) ++ [
             # ./patches/custom.patch  # uncomment if needed
           ];
         })
         ```
      3. Replace PACKAGE_NAME with the actual package name
      4. Keep all package-specific patches in the same directory
      5. Document any non-obvious modifications

examples:
  - input: |
      # Copyright (c) 2024 Geoffrey Huntley <ghuntley@ghuntley.com>. All rights reserved.
      # SPDX-License-Identifier: Proprietary

      { pkgs, ... }:

      pkgs.addlicense.overrideAttrs (old: {
        patches = (old.patches or []) ++ [
          ./patches/custom.patch
        ];
      })
    output: "Correctly structured third-party package overlay"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.1
</rule>
